Speaker separation
-----------------------------

Clipwise separates voices on the call-audio track using the FluidAudio SDK
(https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). The full
license text is reproduced at the end of this file.

FluidAudio runs pyannote's "community-1" speaker diarization pipeline,
converted to Core ML by Fluid Inference. The model files this requires are
licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The
following notice is reproduced verbatim from FluidAudio's own NOTICE.md
(https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/speaker-diarization-coreml/blob/main/NOTICE.md),
which scopes that license to the specific files Clipwise bundles:

    # Attribution and license scope

    This is a mixed-license-scope repository. Fluid Inference intends the
    included CC-BY-4.0 license text to cover only the following exact
    Community-1-derived artifacts and their uncompiled counterparts listed
    in `provenance.json`:

    - `Segmentation.mlmodelc`
    - `FBank.mlmodelc`
    - `Embedding.mlmodelc`
    - `PLDA.mlmodelc`
