Transcription
-----------------------------

NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2 (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2), created by NVIDIA, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Modified: converted to Core ML by FluidInference (https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-coreml).

The transcription engine that runs this model is built with the FluidAudio SDK,
version 0.17.3 (https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, reproduced in full at the end of this file.

Echo cancellation
-----------------------------

When a call is captured on the built-in speakers, Clipwise removes the speaker
echo from the microphone track after the call using WebRTC's AEC3 echo canceller,
from the webrtc-audio-processing library, version 2.1
(https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pulseaudio/webrtc-audio-processing, commit
846fe90a289f58b7c9303a635142aa2c7caa93e5), built statically with the abseil-cpp
library (https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp, 20240722.0, Copyright The Abseil
Authors), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, reproduced in full at
the end of this file. The notices below are those the libraries' own licences
require.

